{
 "id": "grip-pad-finger-mm",
 "kind": "multimat",
 "brief": "A finger for my GRIP robot gripper, printed on a Bambu with the AMS in two materials: a rigid\ncore (PLA, PETG or PA-CF, your call) and a TPU 95A grip pad, printed flat (layers along Z).\nIt pivots on a 3 mm pin along Z at the origin (3.2 mm hole with 2.5 mm of wall round it); the\ndrive link pin is at (12, -8), also along Z, same hole and wall. The finger fits in x = -6 to\n70, y = -14 to 8, z = -5 to 5. The contact face is the +Y face from x = 38 to 70: put a 2 mm\nTPU pad there (y = 6 to 8, full height), all TPU through its thickness, with rigid material\nright behind it, and keep the pin bosses rigid. Loads: hold it at both pins; grip is 20 N on\nthe pad face pushing in -Y; slip is the same squeeze plus 8 N of friction along -X dragging the\npad (that's what peels pads off) and 4 N along Z. Safety factor 2 on the plastic and on the\nbond between the TPU and the core. Under 9 g please.",
 "attachments": [],
